# Put your real key in ONE of these locations (first wins for each variable; shell export still overrides file):
#   ./.pacifico.env                    (current working directory when Pi starts — often your project root)
#   ~/.config/pi/pacifico.env        (recommended global, create ~/.config/pi if needed)
#   ~/.pacifico.env
#   extensions/.pacifico.env         (inside the agent-pi package, next to pacifico.ts)
#
# Quick start from agent-pi repo root:
#   mkdir -p ~/.config/pi && cp extensions/.pacifico.env.example ~/.config/pi/pacifico.env
# Then edit ~/.config/pi/pacifico.env and set PACIFICO_API_KEY (same value as Pacifico .dev.vars / Worker secret, ≥32 chars).

PACIFICO_API_KEY=
# Optional — default is the deployed workers.dev URL:
# PACIFICO_BASE_URL=https://pacifico.example.workers.dev
# Local Worker:
# PACIFICO_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8787
# Optional default model override (otherwise persisted /pacifico-model or backend defaults):
# PACIFICO_MODEL=openai/gpt-5.4-nano
# Legacy name accepted by Pacifico Worker only; prefer PACIFICO_API_KEY:
# HARNESS_API_KEY=
